@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] hostd-no-elevation-or-raw-diagnostics
lilly-hostd MUST run without setuid bits or file capabilities; its systemd
unit supplies its privileges. It writes no log stream: replies carry closed
status and refusal codes only, and utility arguments, output, credential
material and native error strings MUST NOT become diagnostics. Lilly emits
the reviewed events for every effect it requests.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] hostd-closed-utilities
hostd MUST execute only executables from its fixed utility table, resolved
from its own PATH at startup, with a cleared environment (PATH and LC_ALL=C
only) and stdin closed. A caller never supplies an executable path.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] hostd-hegel-properties
Protocol decoding, directory validation and lease ordering MUST be covered
by Hegel property tests against independent models, and session custody
(commands killed and reaped before their lease is released, on release and
on session death) by tests that run real utilities. Tests run without root;
cgroup custody and caller-death fencing of production Lilly paths remain
with the NixOS machine tests.
